{
  "methodId": "cohort-state-transition",
  "entrypointContract": "function(specification) -> {strategyName: {cost: finite number, qaly: finite number}}; preserve every supplied strategy key\nSpecification fields and shapes:\ninitial: Length-N nonnegative finite occupancy vector. Preserve its mass; do not normalize or replace it.\nstrategies: Object keyed by arbitrary strategy names. Evaluate every key independently; keys are not a fixed clinical vocabulary.\ntransitionMatrices: For each strategy, array of T matrices, each N by N. Matrix element [i][j] is the probability of moving from origin i to destination j. Rows sum to one. Matrices are in chronological order and may differ by cycle.\ncostRewards: For each strategy, one static N by N matrix, reused at all T+1 time points. Element [i][j] is cost earned for occupancy flow from origin i to destination j. It is not a cycle-by-state table.\nutilityRewards: Same static N by N flow-reward shape and indexing as costRewards, for QALYs; negative transition rewards are permitted.\ncostWeights: Length T+1 vector. Element 0 weights initial flow; element t weights transition t. Contains the complete supplied discount and correction factors; do not add another correction.\nutilityWeights: Same time indexing and length as costWeights, independently supplied.\nMathematical semantics:\nLet x[0] = initial and F[0][i][j] = initial[i] when i=j, otherwise zero. Initial diagonal flow contributes to both totals.\nFor t=1..T: F[t][i][j] = x[t-1][i] * transitionMatrices[t-1][i][j]; x[t][j] = sum_i F[t][i][j].\ncost = sum_{t=0..T} costWeights[t] * sum_{i,j} F[t][i][j] * costRewards[i][j]. qaly uses utilityWeights and utilityRewards analogously.\nUse every matrix element, including non-diagonal transition rewards. Do not substitute destination occupancy times a single state-reward row.\nReject incompatible dimensions or non-finite inputs clearly; do not guess a different tensor convention. The required interface uses 2D static reward matrices, not 3D reward tensors.\nInput boundaries: Initial occupancy must contain finite non-negative numbers; preserve its supplied total without normalization. Every transition probability must be finite and in [0,1], and each row must sum to 1 within the stated small numerical tolerance. A tolerance is not permission for out-of-range probabilities. Static flow rewards may include negative disutilities or net cost offsets; do not impose the narrower per-state utility convention on flow-reward matrices. Reject malformed dimensions and nonnumeric values rather than calculating.",
  "basis": "Synthetic arithmetic known truth; development examples, not published-paper validation. Include initial diagonal flow rewards; subsequent flows equal prior occupancy times transition probabilities. Reward and discount weights are provided explicitly.",
